# Mapsift build-context filter.
#
# Same rule as .gitignore: exclude what a tool regenerates inside the image, and exclude what
# must never enter an image at all. The difference is the failure mode, so it is worth stating:
# an over-broad entry here is not noise, it is a build that fails at a COPY, or worse, an image
# that silently ships a host-built artifact. Everything a Dockerfile copies has to survive this
# file.

.git
.github

# Secrets never enter an image (ADR-0001 section 4, I7, C6, PRD N3). The templates carry no real
# values and are documentation, so they stay.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.*.example
*.pem
*.p12

# Built inside the image, from the lockfiles that are copied in. Copying a host build in is how a
# container ends up running binaries linked against the host's libraries: node_modules carries
# compiled native modules, .venv hard-codes the interpreter path it was created with, and
# target/ and pkg/ are the Rust and wasm outputs the core stage produces itself.
node_modules
dist
.angular
out-tsc
**/target
**/pkg
**/.venv
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]

# Tool caches, every one rebuilt from what it describes.
.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
.pytest_cache
coverage
htmlcov
*.log

# In no image: the authority chain and the agent configuration are read by people and by Claude
# Code, never by a running service, and the editor prototype carries its own node_modules, its
# own .angular cache and its own git history (PRD section 9 makes it a visual reference, never a
# scaffold).
specs
.claude
tests/prototypes
README.md
CLAUDE.md
